WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.070
Here they are.

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.790
One, no direction.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:08.590
Momentum change in momentum, impulse and force all need a direction.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.850
Or a sign with your positive direction stated.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.390
Two, the bounce.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.570
The ball on your card goes in at 5 metres per second.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.570
It comes back at 3.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.270
The two velocities have opposite signs.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.610
Final minus initial.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:29.870
Negative 3, take away 5, not 3, take away 5.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.910
The examiners wrote this about matric candidates.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:40.070
The change in direction of the ball was often disregarded in the mathematics.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:44.530
So draw a sketch and choose a positive direction.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:46.870
Three, the airbag.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.530
The change in momentum does not get smaller.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.590
The time gets longer.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.590
So the force gets smaller.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:55.370
And a bonus.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:56.990
Milliseconds.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:01.150
20 milliseconds is 0,02 seconds.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.890
Convert before you divide.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.770
Now try the twin on the card.
